# Cursor Rules — MT EMU PCIe DMA Driver Test Generation

You are working on the **MT EMU PCIe DMA Driver** test suite.
This is a Linux kernel + user-space Catch2 test suite for a Synopsys DesignWare-based
PCIe DMA controller (MT/Mthreads GPU/APU devices, vendor 0x1ed5).

## Language & Framework
- Tests are **C++11** using **Catch2** (header-only, in `test/src/catch2/`)
- Every test file must include:
  ```cpp
  #include "catch2/catch.hpp"
  #include "simlog.h"
  #include "mt-emu-drv.h"
  #include "mt_pcie_f.h"
  #include "test_thr.h"
  ```
- Build: `cd test && mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && make`
- Run: `./test -t "[tagname]"`

## Device Function Constants (mt_pcie_f.h)
```c
F_GPU  = 0   // PF0 GPU
F_APU  = 1   // PF1 APU
F_VGUP(i)    // VF i (0..VF_NUM-1)
F_MTDMA      // DMA buffer device
```

## Primary DMA API
```c
// Core transfer — returns 0 on success
int pcief_dma_bare_xfer(
    uint32_t data_direction,  // DMA_MEM_TO_DEV / DMA_DEV_TO_MEM / DMA_DEV_TO_DEV / DMA_MEM_TO_MEM
    uint32_t desc_direction,  // DMA_DESC_IN_DEVICE (0) or DMA_DESC_IN_HOST (1)
    uint32_t desc_cnt,        // N-1 for N descriptors; 0 = single descriptor
    uint32_t block_cnt,       // 0 = no block mode
    uint32_t ch_num,          // channel 0-63
    uint64_t sar,             // source address
    uint64_t dar,             // destination address
    uint32_t size,            // bytes
    uint32_t timeout_ms       // use cal_timeout(size)
);

// BAR access
uint32_t pcief_greg_u32(uint8_t fun, uint8_t bar, uint64_t address);
void     pcief_sreg_u32(uint8_t fun, uint8_t bar, uint64_t address, uint32_t value);

// Host DMA buffer
long pcief_dmabuf_malloc(uint64_t len);   // returns physical addr
void pcief_dmabuf_free(long addr);
```

## Transfer Modes
| Mode | desc_cnt | block_cnt |
|------|----------|-----------|
| Single descriptor | 0 | 0 |
| Chain (N descs) | N-1 | 0 |
| Block (B blocks of D descs) | D-1 | B |

## Direction Bitmask for Multi-Direction Tests
```cpp
uint32_t dirs = BIT(DMA_MEM_TO_DEV) | BIT(DMA_DEV_TO_MEM) | BIT(DMA_DEV_TO_DEV);
```

## Test Helper
```cpp
// Spawns ch_cnt threads, runs transfer, asserts 0 return
void dma_bare_simple_test(
    uint32_t ch_start_num, uint32_t ch_cnt,
    uint32_t data_direction_bits, uint32_t desc_direction,
    uint32_t desc_cnt, uint32_t block_cnt,
    uint64_t device_sar, uint64_t device_dar,
    uint64_t size, int cnt, int offset
);

// Timeout helper (2 MB/s baseline)
static int cal_timeout(uint64_t size);
```

## Test Tag Conventions
- `[mtdma0]` — sanity/smoke (single descriptor)
- `[mtdma1]` — functional (chain, block, sizes, DDR)
- `[mtdma_mmu]` — MMU + DMA
- `[base]` — BAR/ROM access
- `[intr0]` / `[intr1]` — interrupt tests

## Typical Test Case Structure
```cpp
TEST_CASE("descriptive_test_name", "[tag]") {
    LInfo("TEST_CASE descriptive_test_name start\n");

    // set up parameters
    uint32_t ch_num              = 0;
    uint32_t ch_cnt              = 1;
    uint32_t data_direction_bits = BIT(DMA_MEM_TO_DEV) | BIT(DMA_DEV_TO_MEM);
    uint32_t desc_direction      = DMA_DESC_IN_DEVICE;
    uint32_t desc_cnt            = 0;
    uint32_t block_cnt           = 0;
    uint64_t device_sar          = 0x0;
    uint64_t device_dar          = 0x0;
    uint64_t size                = 512 * 1024;
    int      cnt                 = 1;

    dma_bare_simple_test(ch_num, ch_cnt, data_direction_bits,
                         desc_direction, desc_cnt, block_cnt,
                         device_sar, device_dar, size, cnt, 0);

    LInfo("TEST_CASE descriptive_test_name done\n");
}
```

## Device DDR Address Constants (mt-emu-drv.h)
```c
LADDR_MTDMA_TEST   = 0x100000         // general test region
LADDR_APU          = DDR_SZ_FREE      // APU DDR
LADDR_MTDMA_LL_WR  // DMA write-channel link-list region
LADDR_MTDMA_LL_RD  // DMA read-channel link-list region
LADDR_VGPU(vf)     // per-VF 1 GB DDR window
```

## Interrupt Bits (mt-emu-mtdma-bare.h)
```c
DMA_CH_INTR_BIT_DONE           = BIT(0)  // success
DMA_CH_INTR_BIT_ERR_DATA       = BIT(1)  // data error
DMA_CH_INTR_BIT_ERR_DESC_READ  = BIT(2)  // descriptor read error
DMA_CH_INTR_BIT_ERR_CFG        = BIT(3)  // config error
DMA_CH_INTR_BIT_ERR_DUMMY_READ = BIT(4)  // address validation failure
```

## Key Rules
1. `desc_cnt` is always **N−1** (N = total descriptors).
2. `block_cnt = 0` means no block mode.
3. Use `cal_timeout(size)` for timeout; multiply by `block_cnt` for block mode.
4. Use `REQUIRE()` for fatal assertions; never suppress errors silently.
5. Log with `LInfo()` / `LError()`, not bare `printf` (though printf also works).
6. `pcief_init()` is called globally — do **not** call it inside individual test cases.
7. For multi-channel tests, `dma_bare_simple_test` automatically offsets device addresses by `size` per channel.
8. For all-direction tests use the bitmask: `BIT(DMA_MEM_TO_DEV)|BIT(DMA_DEV_TO_MEM)|BIT(DMA_DEV_TO_DEV)|BIT(DMA_MEM_TO_MEM)`.
9. New test `.cc` files in `test/src/` are automatically picked up by CMake (`file(GLOB TEST_SOURCES src/*.cc)`).
10. Existing test files are `base.cc`, `mthdma.cc`, `intr.cc`, `stress.cc` — add new tests in the appropriate file or create a new file.
